# MUST BE INCONSISTENT: ActionPath and Action are disjoint. IEC 60050-351,
# 351-44-03 defines a path as structure, a directed path connecting two
# variable quantities, and 351-42-24 an action as behaviour, the influence of
# one variable quantity on another. Keeping them apart is what lets the
# pattern tell a closed path from a closed action.
@prefix iec60050: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#> .
@prefix inst:     <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050/instances#> .
@prefix ex:       <https://w3id.org/aias/example/iec60050/neg#> .
@prefix owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/example/iec60050/neg01> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050/instances/1.0.0> .
ex:Thing1 a iec60050:ActionPath , iec60050:Action .
